From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Maus <mail@jens-maus.de>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: misc: onboard_usb_dev: add Microchip LAN9514

The LAN9514 (USB 0424:9514) combines a USB 2.0 hub and a 10/100
Ethernet controller in one chip. It is the onboard hub of the
Raspberry Pi 2 Model B and 3 Model B, where its nRESET input is
driven by a GPIO named LAN_RUN.

On these boards the chip stays powered across a warm reboot. Only the
SoC is reset, so the chip is never reset unless the firmware does it,
and the firmware does not do it reliably. Now and then the chip then
does not answer the next USB bus reset: no hub, no Ethernet and no USB
devices until a power cycle.

Let onboard_usb_dev manage the chip, so that a "reset-gpios" property
on its device-tree node gives it a defined hardware reset whenever the
kernel boots, independent of how the previous system went down. The
10 ms pulse matches what phy-generic uses for the same chip on the
OMAP4 PandaBoard.
---
 drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c | 1 +
 drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
index 41360a7..8b29698 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.c
@@ -666,6 +666,7 @@ static const struct usb_device_id onboard_dev_id_table[] = {
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_MICROCHIP, 0x2517) }, /* USB2517 USB 2.0 HUB */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_MICROCHIP, 0x2744) }, /* USB5744 USB 2.0 HUB */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_MICROCHIP, 0x5744) }, /* USB5744 USB 3.0 HUB */
+	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_MICROCHIP, 0x9514) }, /* LAN9514 USB 2.0 HUB */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_PARADE, 0x5511) }, /* PS5511 USB 3.2 */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_PARADE, 0x55a1) }, /* PS5511 USB 2.0 */
 	{ USB_DEVICE(VENDOR_ID_REALTEK, 0x0411) }, /* RTS5411 USB 3.1 HUB */
diff --git a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h
index c1462be..4764825 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/misc/onboard_usb_dev.h
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@ static const struct onboard_dev_pdata microchip_usb2514_data = {
 	.is_hub = true,
 };
 
+static const struct onboard_dev_pdata microchip_lan9514_data = {
+	.reset_us = 10000,
+	.num_supplies = 1,
+	.supply_names = { "vdd" },
+	.is_hub = true,
+};
+
 static const struct onboard_dev_pdata microchip_usb5744_data = {
 	.reset_us = 0,
 	.power_on_delay_us = 10000,
@@ -128,6 +135,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id onboard_dev_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "usb424,2517", .data = &microchip_usb424_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb424,2744", .data = &microchip_usb5744_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb424,5744", .data = &microchip_usb5744_data, },
+	{ .compatible = "usb424,9514", .data = &microchip_lan9514_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb451,8025", .data = &ti_tusb8020b_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb451,8027", .data = &ti_tusb8020b_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "usb451,8140", .data = &ti_tusb8041_data, },
